---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
---
<Legal title="Cookie Policy" path="/cookies">
  <p class="callout">
    <strong>Please note:</strong> This is a starting template. Update it to reflect the exact cookies and
    analytics tools you actually deploy, and have it reviewed by a qualified attorney.
  </p>

  <p>
    This Cookie Policy explains how IV Salt Rejuvenation uses cookies and similar technologies on our website.
  </p>

  <h2>What Are Cookies?</h2>
  <p>
    Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help websites work,
    remember your preferences, and understand how the site is used.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Cookies</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> — required for the website and booking flow to function.</li>
    <li><strong>Preference cookies</strong> — remember choices you make to improve your experience.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> — help us understand how visitors use the site so we can improve it.
      These are only set if we enable an analytics tool.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Our website is designed to be privacy-friendly. We self-host our fonts and avoid unnecessary third-party
    tracking. We do not use cookies to sell your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>
    Some features rely on trusted third parties that may set their own cookies, such as our booking, consent
    form, and payment providers. Their use of cookies is governed by their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Managing Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can control and delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking some cookies may affect how the
    website and booking flow work. Most browsers let you refuse or delete cookies via their preferences menu.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update this Cookie Policy as our website evolves. The "last updated" date above reflects the latest revision.</p>
</Legal>
